WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.000
Hey everyone Diavolo here and&nbsp;
today were back at it with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.080
pinnacle of all domain videos. In this&nbsp;
we are going to cover all of the known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.040
domains that have been introduced to&nbsp;
us or mentioned throughout the series.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.160
A Domain Expansion is the most incomparable&nbsp;
technique of any jujutsu user. It is the peak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.600
of their essence, all pulled forth and&nbsp;
imagined through an innate domain that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.640
itself, is covered with a barrier to&nbsp;
construct it in a different space.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.720
With Jujutsu sorcery hand signs,&nbsp;
words, dance and other forms of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.920
expressions all expand the level to&nbsp;
which someone can manipulate cursed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.720
energy. A domain expansion is expanded&nbsp;
through the use of one of these actions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:43.050
for example Mahito opens his mouth wide to perform&nbsp;
his, while Dagon forms a symbol on their torso.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:46.000
(Coffin Of The Iron Mountain) First of the&nbsp;
domains that we see throughout the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.480
Coffin Of The Iron Mountain is the special&nbsp;
grade disaster curse, Jogoat’s supreme art.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.680
This fiery domain meticulously replicates&nbsp;
the inner sanctum of a roaring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.200
live volcano. Encased within an impenetrable&nbsp;
stone chamber, its colossal walls and floors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.080
are riddled with gaping crevices that&nbsp;
gush forth copious amounts of molten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:09.200
magma. This results in a temperature so&nbsp;
insanely hot, that any typical jujutsu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:14.160
user would instantly succumb to spontaneous&nbsp;
combustion upon setting foot within the domain.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.480
Fittingly dubbed the "Coffin of the Iron&nbsp;
Mountain," this a lethal type domain that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.400
is a equipped with a guaranteed hit. To&nbsp;
activate the lethal sure hit technique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.080
the user can control with ease all&nbsp;
of the lava and molten rock flowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:29.840
around the inside of the domain, and&nbsp;
direct that towards their target.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.640
(Unlimited Void) Seen right after&nbsp;
we witnessed the Iron Mountain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.600
Unlimited Void is one of, if not the&nbsp;
most advanced technique in the vast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:42.640
arsenal of the Limitless. Due to being the&nbsp;
stronger and more refined of the two domain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:47.280
Gojo’s Unlimited Void easily overpowered&nbsp;
and suppressed the effects of Jogo’s.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.040
When it comes to the effects of Unlimited&nbsp;
Void, this domain inserts the user and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.560
their intended targets inside "Limitless Itself,"&nbsp;
a boundless void filled with infinite flowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:00.640
knowledge. Within this vast space, a constant&nbsp;
flow of complex information floods into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.680
minds of the targets, overwhelming them to the&nbsp;
extent that they become completely paralyzed.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.320
The incapacitation of the target occurs due to&nbsp;
a unique phenomenon where the target is both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.720
aware of everything and yet unable to perceive&nbsp;
or sense anything at the same time. It's as if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:20.400
every action they've ever taken in their life&nbsp;
is repeatedly imposed upon them, causing them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.160
suffer a slow and inevitable demise. It's worth&nbsp;
noting that this effect doesn't impact the user&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.960
or anyone they are in physical contact with. So&nbsp;
if you were to be stuck in this domain, the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:35.940
way to survive would be getting ahold of Gojo or&nbsp;
repairing that destroyed brain of yours with RCT.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:40.920
(Self Embodiment Of Perfection) Third up,&nbsp;
and nearing the final seconds of Mahito’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:45.280
battle against Nanami and Yuji, he was able&nbsp;
to discover something by using his death as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:51.000
an inspiration. Opening his mouth, Mahito throws&nbsp;
up miniature gang sign hand seals formed by tiny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:56.640
hands inside of his mouth to activate his Domain&nbsp;
Expansion, The Self Embodiment Of Perfection.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.800
This infamous domain creates a vast, dark space&nbsp;
where Mahito's target encounters enormous hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.040
that come together to form a flower-like&nbsp;
shape. These giant hands are connected by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:11.000
multiple arms, creating a net-like cage&nbsp;
that encircles Mahito's intended victim.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.280
The Self-Embodiment of Perfection works by&nbsp;
amplifying the effectiveness of Mahito's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.360
Cursed Technique, Idle Transfiguration and&nbsp;
ensuring it directly affects the target's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:23.840
soul instantly. Being inside of the Self&nbsp;
Embodiment of Perfection is described as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:30.040
feeling as if you're figuratively in the palm of&nbsp;
Mahito's. Due to how idle transfiguration works,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:34.800
this Domain Expansion is an almost sure kill&nbsp;
type of domain expansion. The only way one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.320
would survive, is if they had some form of ability&nbsp;
that allowed them to block damage to their soul.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.800
One thing I wanna point out about&nbsp;
Domain Expansions. If given time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.440
a Domain user can easily decide&nbsp;
who is caught by their domain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.320
as we saw with Mahito’s first bout&nbsp;
against Yuji and Nanami. However though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:55.960
when the preparation time is extremely limited,&nbsp;
or the conditions changed, one cant specifically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.960 --> 00:04:00.760
chose who is caught by it. This here, can&nbsp;
lead to a few drawbacks of Mahito’s domain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:07.160
and if he does accidentally touch the wrong&nbsp;
soul, it can backfire with drastic consequences.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:12.440
(Graveyard) Using its fingers to craft hand&nbsp;
signs, the Smallpox Deity can active their domain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:17.160
Graveyard and instantly trap an opponent&nbsp;
inside. As the name suggests, the domain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.920
itself is just a graveyard. What's special&nbsp;
about it though is how it plays on the curses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:27.000
innate Gravestone Technique. Due to a domain&nbsp;
usually being granted with an automatic-hit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.680
Graveyard enhances the cursed technique and&nbsp;
automatically traps the opponent with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:35.720
highest cursed energy output in a coffin. Then,&nbsp;
once the conditions are fulfilled it guarantee’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:40.480
that the person will be infected with smallpox&nbsp;
and die. These conditions are that the curse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:46.400
has to count down from 3, if it reaches one,&nbsp;
then it wins. If someone escapes the coffin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:51.760
it can continuously use this sure hit&nbsp;
technique over and over again. On top of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:56.936
the gravestone itself deals critical&nbsp;
damage when putting someone underground.

00:04:56.936 --> 00:04:59.560
(Chimera Shadow Garden) Next up and I&nbsp;
somehow initially forgot that we saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:03.640
Megumi’s first use of his domain during&nbsp;
the last few moments during season 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:07.760
Although not fully able to be constructed&nbsp;
inside a sphere, Chimera Shadow Garden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.800
when expelled in an environment that allows&nbsp;
it, saturates the surroundings with dense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:15.960
shadowy liquid. This allows any user&nbsp;
of the Ten Shadows Technique to summon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:21.240
multiple shikigami at once and have free&nbsp;
manipulation over all shadows in the area.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:25.240
Additionally, it brings forth a&nbsp;
sizable structure resembling two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:29.760
columns of spinal bone interconnected&nbsp;
by some form of nerve endings. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:33.960
this object vanishes shortly after&nbsp;
the initial activation of the domain.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.680
Anyone standing in the shadow will have to&nbsp;
reinforce their feet with cursed energy or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:44.800
risk falling into the abyss, this includes the&nbsp;
user themselves. Within the liquid-like shadows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:49.120
there is no buoyancy, resistance, or&nbsp;
oxygen. Anyone who has dropped into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.280
it will fall indefinitely. AAAAAAND I&nbsp;
WONDER WHERE MEGUMI CURRENTLY IS....

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:58.160
(Horizon Of The Captivating Skandha)&nbsp;
Dagon's Domain Expansion, Horizon Of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:01.840
The Captivating Skandha is activated&nbsp;
like I said earlier in the video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:06.560
with a seal on his stomach. This results&nbsp;
in the creation of a serene tropical beach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:11.600
type domain. This domain is often described as&nbsp;
peaceful, and the water near the beach is shallow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:16.320
enough for someone to stand in. This domain did&nbsp;
actually make an appearance during season 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.640
however it was only for a moment, while&nbsp;
Dagon was still in his cursed womb state.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:25.640
Within the Horizon of the Captivating Skandha,&nbsp;
Dagon's innate technique that ensures the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:30.280
shikigami crafted by him automatically strike&nbsp;
their designated target. From the perspective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:35.240
of those being targeted, these fish-like&nbsp;
shikigami seemingly materialize out of nowhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.520
making them exceptionally hard&nbsp;
to predict. This is because the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:43.960
shikigami only come into existence at the&nbsp;
moment they make contact with the target.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:48.240
One of the techniques inside of Dagon's domain&nbsp;
that takes advantage of this sure hit effect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:53.440
Death Swarm takes the form of large marine&nbsp;
like shikigami and has them constantly attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:57.560
until the opponent is devoured. The only&nbsp;
way to stop this endless sea of death is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:02.940
to disrupt the cursed spirits domain and&nbsp;
glitch out the sure hit function of it.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:09.600
(Malevolent Shrine) True to its name, the&nbsp;
Malevolent Shrine creates an area focused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:14.280
around a small singular, altered Buddhist&nbsp;
shrine, that has been distorted to instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:19.080
enshrine demons. This shrine somewhat&nbsp;
resembles a Chinjudō and if you remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:23.360
back to where exactly Megumi was looking&nbsp;
for Sukuna’s finger during the early EP’s.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:32.880
Anyways Anyways, Instead of the peaceful&nbsp;
picturesque shrines peaceful deities have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:37.480
Sukuna’s shrine (or the FREAKING KITCHEN as&nbsp;
someone at Crunchyroll decided to mess up),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:43.760
is encircled by murky, dark-colored water, and&nbsp;
the ground is adorned with horned skulls. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:49.080
roof is embellished with protruding horns and&nbsp;
suspended human skulls. The four entrances to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:54.760
the shrine take the form of large, grotesque&nbsp;
mouths, featuring humanlike teeth and tongues.

00:07:54.760 --> 00:08:00.080
Unlike almost every other domain seen so far in&nbsp;
the series, Sukuna’s domain is built different.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:04.320
Instead of imagining an innate environment&nbsp;
and surrounding it with a barrier to give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:10.720
it structure. The KING of curses, Ryomen Sukuna is&nbsp;
equipped with a barrier-less domain. An art so far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:16.440
beyond normal comprehension its as if someone is&nbsp;
painting in thin air without the use of a canvas.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:20.240
The Malevolent Shrine's guaranteed-hit&nbsp;
ability enables it to ruthlessly slash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:24.600
through anything within its effective&nbsp;
range until only dust remains. To do this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:30.040
Sukuna employs two types of slashing attacks,&nbsp;
namely his known and extremely trusty Cleave and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:35.400
Dismantle. These two slicing attacks will not stop&nbsp;
slashing until the domain is disengaged or Sukuna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:41.640
is too severely injured to sustain it any longer.&nbsp;
Sukuna has the capability to choose between these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:46.920
two attacks based on the target type, opting for&nbsp;
Dismantle against inanimate objects and Cleave for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:59.160
subjects with cursed energy. This is also how&nbsp;
Sukuna cuts the world for any one confused, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:16.040
uses dismantle to cut the world behind the&nbsp;
infinity. Get it? Also on top of that we’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:21.160
seen Sukuna implement a few different conditions&nbsp;
into the structure of how his domain is formed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:25.720
For example during his battle against Gojo,&nbsp;
Sukuna’s domain grew beyond Unlimited Void's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:30.920
barrier. With a domain's barrier being weak to&nbsp;
attacks on its outer shell, Gojo's domain was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:35.360
crushed by Malevolent Shrine's slashing attacks&nbsp;
and he was immediately struck by its can't-miss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:39.920
attack. Throughout that long battle, some of&nbsp;
the binding vows he placed apon his domain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:43.560
were like removing Malevolent Shrine's&nbsp;
guaranteed-hit effect within Unlimited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:48.360
Void's effective area or narrowing down its&nbsp;
effective range, similar to when it was used in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:56.480
Shibuya. In exchange Sukuna was granted increased&nbsp;
power to counter Gojo’s own domain improvisations.

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:02.560
I didnt mention those improvisations during&nbsp;
Gojo’s infinite void part of the video as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:06.440
they technically qualify as binding vows&nbsp;
that I’ll stick in a binding vow video.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:13.080
Seeing as were here now though... Simply Gojo&nbsp;
could do a bunch of similar improvisations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:17.160
like expanding the Domains Shell or reducing&nbsp;
the overall size of his domain expansion to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:21.640
a basketball, something most&nbsp;
sorcerers deemed impossible.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:30.240
(Deadly Sentencing) 7th of the known domains&nbsp;
that weve seen throughout the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:34.600
comes from the first opponent our main&nbsp;
cast face’s during the culling game.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:38.840
Hiromi Higuruma’s domain Deadly Sentencing&nbsp;
creates a large courtroom where the user&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:43.520
and their target stand across from one another&nbsp;
playing the roles of prosecutor and defendant.

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:47.920
Unlike most of the domains we’ve seen throughout&nbsp;
the series and just due to Higuruma learning the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:53.600
use of his technique in private. Deadly Sentencing&nbsp;
is a type of domain that isn't considered lethal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:58.120
it can still be lethal in the end, but&nbsp;
it doesn't contain a cannot miss attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:03.400
like others. Way back in the early days of&nbsp;
Jujutsu discovery, like before even Sukuna,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:06.800
a domain expansion wasn't used as a&nbsp;
finishing move, instead they forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:11.760
those who were caught inside to abide by the&nbsp;
rules or bindings of that domains technique.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:16.960
Once caught inside of Deadly Sentencing,&nbsp;
the law type cursed technique imbued into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:21.800
the domain allows the user to prosecute their&nbsp;
target with the shikigami called Judgeman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:26.280
Inside this domain, no physical violence&nbsp;
is permitted for either party. Initially,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:31.840
Judgeman reveals the accusations against&nbsp;
the accused, which consist of real crimes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:36.360
they may or may not have committed. Despite&nbsp;
Judgeman having access to all information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:40.280
about everyone within the domain, this&nbsp;
knowledge is not given to the user.

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:45.920
In the trial, the final decision depends on what&nbsp;
each side says. After hearing the accusations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:50.640
the person being accused gets one shot to defend&nbsp;
themselves. They can choose to stay quiet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:58.320
admit guilt, or say they didn't do it. If they&nbsp;
deny it, they can even lie. The goal for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:02.640
accused person is to convince Judgeman&nbsp;
they're innocent and clear any doubts.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:08.440
Once it's the prosecutor's turn in the Deadly&nbsp;
Sentencing, they get a single chance to speak.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:13.160
Their statement is like a counterargument using&nbsp;
evidence given by Judgeman for review. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:18.480
evidence comes in a sealed envelope, held by the&nbsp;
prosecutor. The information inside isn't treated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:23.360
as definite proof, and it stays closed until after&nbsp;
the prosecutor speaks, keeping the accused in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:28.720
the dark. However, Judgeman shares the info with&nbsp;
the prosecutor as soon as they get the envelope.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:33.560
After both the prosecutor and the defense have&nbsp;
had their say, Judgeman steps in to give a legal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:38.800
verdict. If the accused is deemed guilty,&nbsp;
they face one of several possible sentences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:44.240
though the user isn't certain which one.&nbsp;
The severity of the punishment can vary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:48.280
with more serious crimes leading to&nbsp;
harsher penalties in certain cases.

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:55.560
Before the verdict is given, Judgeman often&nbsp;
dishes out a punishment called "Confiscation,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:59.960
which stops the guilty person from using&nbsp;
cursed techniques. Once the verdict is given,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.680
the domain expansion disappears, and the&nbsp;
punishment takes effect on the guilty party&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:08.520
straight away. However, if the accused is&nbsp;
found guilty without openly admitting it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:11.960
they can ask for another trial,&nbsp;
and Judgeman has to agree. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:15.040
is called an appeal and even though&nbsp;
it hasn't specifically been stated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:19.960
im assuming someone has the right to at least 2&nbsp;
appeals, just like we do in most court systems.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:25.120
(Idle Death Gamble) So... When it comes&nbsp;
to this next expansion, Idle Death Gamble,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:30.040
we are prooobably gonna be here a while. This&nbsp;
technique is so hard for my small brain to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:33.600
wrap itself around. It really is one of&nbsp;
the most mind boggling techniques seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:38.760
so far from jujutsu kaisen. Its not crazy,&nbsp;
blowing up cities level of mind boggling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:46.440
but Hakari just had to go and be a creative&nbsp;
genius with way to much time on his hands.&nbsp;

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:50.560
Firstly the full name for this&nbsp;
domain is Idle Death Gamble:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:58.320
CR Private Pure Love Train Version 1/239. The CR&nbsp;
stands for Card Reader and its actually based on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:03.520
a real pachinko machine, with obviously&nbsp;
the same name. Dude is a degenerative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:09.360
manga reader or gambler, probably both.
The user's goal is to hit the jackpot by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:14.400
lining up three of the same symbols decorated&nbsp;
with the characters of Private Pure Love Train.

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:18.440
There are 7 different characters in the private&nbsp;
pure love train series. Starting from the main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:25.680
hero with the number 7, Yuki Yamaguchi. The Main&nbsp;
heroine and number 3, Yume Asagiri. Number 6 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:28.315
Yuki’s younger sister, Sayaka Yamaguchi. According&nbsp;
to info she pretends to be using an electronic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.315 --> 00:14:31.000
dictionary but is jamming on the DS instead.&nbsp;
Number 4 and the dude who cant tell the different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:36.880
between a guitar and a bass, Hiro Kato. Yuki’s&nbsp;
current boss, by day she’s a project manager, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:51.920
when night arrives, damn gurl! The number 2 Sayuri&nbsp;
Amanogawa. Yuki’s current coworker and number 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:58.680
Suzuka Shimizu. Then finally Number 1, Yuki’s&nbsp;
old friend and currently a bank thief, Aya Saito.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:04.160
Now that the characters are all out of&nbsp;
the way, once a jackpot is achieved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:08.920
it grants the user unlimited cursed energy. Along&nbsp;
with that it gives them a fully automatic reversed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:15.200
cursed technique that lasts for exactly 4 minutes&nbsp;
and 11 seconds. The reason for the length of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:21.560
technique is because the theme some for Private&nbsp;
Pure Love Train “Admiring You” runs for that time.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:27.120
To hit the mentioned jackpot, the user needs to&nbsp;
engage actively in the game's dynamics, facing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:37.400
slim 1/239 odds. Once the domain is activated,&nbsp;
the rules of the game are instantaneously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:42.120
transferred to the opponent's mind. This is done&nbsp;
through taking advantage of a domains sure hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:47.400
technique, so Hakari uses the sure hit to transfer&nbsp;
the rules and not to damage. As a trade-off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:53.040
the construction and infusion of cursed technique&nbsp;
into this domain happens unrealistically fast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:58.840
completing in less than 0.2 seconds. Man could&nbsp;
probably stop all those crafty 0.2 second domains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:05.960
from Shibuya. Plus along that same line&nbsp;
of thinking, and just due to how quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:10.920
he can throw up his gang signs, it makes this&nbsp;
domain extremely proficient in activating first.

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:17.480
Moving onto the dynamics of how the game works&nbsp;
inside of a domain. Initially once started,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:21.520
the two opponents will both appear on a&nbsp;
neutral stage. Before they throw hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:26.040
the user has the ability to create three&nbsp;
distinct visual effect indicators: shutter doors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:31.160
reserve balls, and consecutive effects. The&nbsp;
doors and balls serve as offensive maneuvers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:36.520
while consecutive effects act as defensive&nbsp;
indicators, rewinding a sequence to undo damage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:41.520
Doors and reserve balls come in a green, red,&nbsp;
or gold rarity to symbolize a higher chance at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:47.400
a jackpot. Rainbow-colored indicators or re-doing&nbsp;
four consecutive effects guarantees a jackpot.&nbsp;

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:51.800
The user has the option to select&nbsp;
which visual indicator to generate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:57.160
but the outcome is left to chance. Creating one&nbsp;
or more visual indicators advances the stage to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:02.040
a riichi scenario, unveiling two out of&nbsp;
three necessary numbers for a jackpot.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:07.320
When it comes to this new thing I just brought up,&nbsp;
Riichi scenario’s. These are scenarios involving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:11.960
the aforementioned characters from the pure&nbsp;
private love train pachinko machine. From what we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:17.080
have seen, there are 4 different riichi sequences&nbsp;
with differing chances of hitting a jackpot. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:22.440
final train scenario is different though and&nbsp;
has an over 80% chance of jackpot. Each of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:27.320
sequences will change the layout of the domain,&nbsp;
changing it to resemble a different stage, then it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:32.480
will use the characters of Private Pure Love Train&nbsp;
in a different way for that scene. Im not going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:37.960
go over the differing scenario’s in themselves&nbsp;
otherwise, oml we are gonna be here a while.

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:41.200
This is for fact that we haven't even&nbsp;
been able to discuss, what the hell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:45.880
happens if Hakari fails to hit a jackpot.&nbsp;
Pretty much because, like a true gambler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:50.640
Hakari understands that the house always&nbsp;
wins. If someone fails to hit a jackpot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:55.280
then the scenario will revert the stage back to&nbsp;
its original form. This cycle continues until the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.280 --> 00:18:00.120
user either secures a victory or exhausts all&nbsp;
chances to do so, with the number of possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:04.640
attempts diminishing with each unsuccessful&nbsp;
jackpot. During the initial activation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:09.520
consecutive expansions, the likelihood of&nbsp;
hitting the jackpot exceeds twenty percent.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:14.520
When a jackpot is achieved, the domain vanishes,&nbsp;
and “Admiring You“ begins its 4 minutes and 11&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:19.600
second counter, playing loudly around the user.&nbsp;
Like I mentioned to start with, the user receive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:24.200
a bonus of unlimited cursed energy for the&nbsp;
entire duration of the song. This unrestricted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:29.000
cursed energy comes with no limitations, )so&nbsp;
for those few minutes he’s considered special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:32.920
grade) and the user can receive additional&nbsp;
bonus amounts at random intervals throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:38.080
the round. This along with the automatic&nbsp;
use of RCT prevents the user's body from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:43.520
sustaining damage and renders them effectively&nbsp;
invulnerable for four minutes and eleven seconds.

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:47.480
Once the song comes to an end, the user's&nbsp;
cursed energy returns to its normal level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:51.880
and their cursed technique is fully replenished.&nbsp;
This in turn allows them to activate their domain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:57.160
repeatedly, on the condition that they achieve&nbsp;
a jackpot each time. With consecutive uses of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.160 --> 00:19:02.080
this domain, the conditions of the previous one’s&nbsp;
will still be active. If If the user aligns three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:07.160
odd numbers, the stage begins with advanced&nbsp;
probability rather than the neutral state.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:12.120
In the case of aligning even numbers, the stage&nbsp;
commences with faster spins. Meaning that he can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:17.280
bring about a jackpot quicker, even with a less of&nbsp;
a percentage. Additionally, there's a possibility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:22.920
for the stage to start in hidden probability mode.&nbsp;
This is taken directly from a pachinko machine and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:28.360
is usually akin to faster spins but with an&nbsp;
elevated probability of hitting the jackpot.

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:34.160
Thats kind of everything we know about the domain&nbsp;
expansion. Its nice having the binding vow of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:40.240
“showing ones hand”, means we all at some point&nbsp;
or another will get an explanation of an ability.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:46.856
Unless the sorcerer is so much stronger, they&nbsp;
dont even need to mention it. Anyways Anyways!

00:19:46.856 --> 00:19:49.680
(Time Cell Moon Palace) Professional&nbsp;
hater Naoya Zenin came back with one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:54.920
the craziest powerups in the series! His awe&nbsp;
inspiring Domain Expansion fittingly named,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:59.520
Time Cell Moon Palace is my favorite&nbsp;
name for an ability seen in the series.

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:04.800
Unlike the previous few domains we’ve been over,&nbsp;
casting Naoya’s domain is pretty stock standard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:10.560
It creates a black empty environment, like most&nbsp;
other sorcerers, with a few floating organisms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:17.000
seen about. In the center is a large main stage&nbsp;
that is made up of a flesh like substance. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:21.360
pathway leads down to a large eye that&nbsp;
is situated directly behind the caster.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:25.880
The domain's auto-hit feature sends out an&nbsp;
injecting tape of animation frames that jabs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:30.800
into the necks of its chosen targets. If anyone&nbsp;
makes a single movement inside of the domain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:35.160
they must adhere by the 24 FPS rule&nbsp;
of projection sorcerery. If they dont&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:39.080
follow those rules, then unlike the original&nbsp;
technique, they dont get stuck in a frame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:43.120
instead it will result in body&nbsp;
wide injuries on a cellular level.

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:48.520
Like most domains, Time Cell Moon Palace enhances&nbsp;
the accuracy of the embedded cursed technique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:53.280
honing in on individual cells. Freezing&nbsp;
these individual cells disrupts their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:58.520
normal functioning, resulting in innumerable&nbsp;
tiny cuts across the entire body, rendering the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:05.560
target immobile. Any attempt to force movement&nbsp;
may lead to the severing of an entire limb.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:12.863
This is an extremely lethal domain, however&nbsp;
sadly for Naoya dude got hit by a building.

00:21:12.863 --> 00:21:16.120
(Womb Profusion) Next up and second&nbsp;
to last in all of the known domains,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:22.640
Womb Profusion is a terrifyingly deadly ability&nbsp;
in the hands of no one other than Kenjaku himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:27.520
As we saw with Sukuna and just due to how&nbsp;
the battle was playing out against Yuki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:27.520 --> 00:21:31.720
Kenjaku can expand his domain without&nbsp;
enclosing it inside of a barrier.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:35.560
Im assuming that its also possible&nbsp;
for him to enclose it in a barrier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:39.880
but because of how Tengen was targeting&nbsp;
barriers, he purposely decided not to use one.

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:45.200
To activate this domain, the user places the&nbsp;
backside of their fingers together and interlocks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:50.280
them. Enlarging this domain gives rise to a totem&nbsp;
like tower covered in grotesque, merged faces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:54.880
resembling cursed spirits. Anyone ensnared&nbsp;
within the reach of its unavoidable strike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:54.880 --> 00:22:00.640
experiences an explosive impact akin to a direct&nbsp;
hit from Maximum: Uzumaki, although the specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:00.640 --> 00:22:07.120
characteristics of this attack remain undisclosed.&nbsp;
Just because of the curse spirit styling of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:12.400
domain, I believe that its most likely the domain&nbsp;
Suguru could’ve achieved if he didnt pass on.

00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:19.400
(Threefold Affliction) Last now of the known&nbsp;
domains inside of Jujutsu Kaisen. Yorozu’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:24.240
Threefold Affliction is not actually deadly&nbsp;
in itself, instead this domain’s sure-hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:24.240 --> 00:22:29.080
